pipeline='''# Asset Pipeline

Active Phase 2 strategy: immutable downloaded source → read-only audit and isolated Asset Lab → verified working derivatives → curated public/assets promotion → visual children attached to existing gameplay roots. SOURCE_ASSETS and REFERENCES remain outside production; ASSET_WORK stores ignored experiments/evidence. All 1,092 protected files match source hashes.

Cartoon Boy has zero supplied clips: its repaired 100-joint rig and 75 morph channels use authored local poses. Mountain's 95-joint downloaded Young model preserves Take 001 but gameplay motion uses authored local bones, separate from physics/root motion. Existing Baby and Guardian procedural geometry remains explicit unfinished/fallback content. Eggs stay procedural. RuntimeAssets caches templates and uses SkeletonUtils for independent rigs, with tested disposal/retry/late-load ownership.

Sanctuary uses selected Village body/body2/tower/flag/cart and V01 Market around existing service/collision positions. Stone maps use low-poly tiled planes, Normal GL, ARM-G roughness and correctly normalized 16-bit AO. Source high-poly material-preview geometry is not placed as road. BASE_URL prefixes production model/map loads; no new compression decoder is required.

The dev-only [Asset Lab](../../asset-lab.html) supports GLTFLoader and FBXLoader with neutral comparisons, individual normalized clip playback, safe dependencies, statistics and errors. Development middleware checks allowlists and real paths. `.gltfbuffer` aliases original `.bin` reads to avoid this machine's IDM interception; originals never rename. Production builds only index.html and expose no raw-source/working routes or lab entry.

The historical [Nature Young GLB](../../public/assets/models/dragons/3d-young-dragon-nature.glb) remains unchanged: 5,236,028 bytes, SHA-256 b2e0f29c1e238efc8cba8a6435cd12c201acb7a8df06ce5d02cb79b77130c615. Its static no-skin/no-clip mesh is never fetched by gameplay. All original PNG references retain names/hashes.

See [tool commands](../../tools/asset-pipeline/README.md), [all-source validation](ASSET_VALIDATION_REPORT.md), [canonical sources/settings/outputs](ASSET_RUNTIME_PLAN.md), [gameplay and performance evidence](ASSET_INTEGRATION_REPORT.md), and [runtime attribution](../../public/assets/ATTRIBUTION.md). Technical readiness, local gameplay integration and usage status are independent. Failed exports stay outside public. Adult, other elements, final audio/music and other creature families remain deferred.
'''
(ROOT/'DOCS/TECHNICAL/ASSET_PIPELINE.md').write_text(pipeline,encoding='utf8')
